<article class="env-lemma" id="0GX7">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GX7">Lemma <span data-tag="0GX7">87.5.8</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a continuous homomorphism of linearly topologized rings. If $\varphi $ is taut and $A$ is weakly pre-admissible, then $B$ is weakly pre-admissible. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $I \subset A$ be a weak ideal of definition. Then the closure $J$ of $IB$ is open and consists of topologically nilpotent elements by Lemma <a href="/tag/0AMW" data-tag="0AMW">87.4.10</a>. Hence $J$ is a weak ideal of definition of $B$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>